From f5c1c968aff12b3e8e01e6d7a070c710efca5678 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:42:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 184/214] feat: shade ray hits with CE's own forward lighting
 (stage 2A, shaders)

A triangle hit stops being a guess and becomes a lit surface. ConeTracePS now
writes intermediate g-data instead of a provisional colour, and a new ShadePass
technique turns that g-data back into the ALD + RGB contract DemosaicPass and
UpScalePass already speak, so nothing downstream changes.

- Total_Illumination_Shading.cfi (new): CE's TiledForwardShading and
  Fwd_StandardOpaqueShading copied with the four substitutions of decision 06 -
  a world-space light-mask grid instead of the screen tile mask, viewVec =
  -RayDirection, Fwd_SampleSunShadowMaps(worldPos) instead of the reflecting
  pixel's screen-space shadow mask, and g-data instead of the G-buffer. Two of
  Neo's gaps fixed on the way in: the grid cell index is clamped to the grid
  box, and the builder stores instead of InterlockedOr-ing so a stale mask
  cannot survive a frame. bOpaque is always false at a hit: AO, the shadow mask
  and ApplyGI would all be screen-space reads of the wrong pixel. Area lights
  are skipped as Neo does.
- BuildRayTracingLightListCS lives here too, not in TiledShading.cfi, because
  that file's technique region is inside #if TILED_DEFERRED_SHADING_TECHNIQUE
  and a technique outside it would be emitted into every material shader.
- Total_Illumination.cfx: CustomForwardShadingAttribs and Callback_ShadingDirect
  before the includes; ForwardShading.cfi pulled in ahead of CommonSVO.cfi so
  CBPerPassForward (b5) is declared before ApplyGI reads cbSVOGI; pixoutMRTTrace
  gains HITPOS (RGBA32F, camera-relative, .w = smoothness) and RAYDIR (.w = hit
  distance, GetMaxRayDistance()+1 on a miss) under %_RT_QUALITY; ShadePS and the
  two new techniques; refl_GAL/GNO/GPO/GLD on t0-t3 with the aliasing warning.
- Exposure: the hit is lit by already-exposed lights, so ShadePS divides by
  PS_HDR_RANGE_ADAPT_MAX before writing, leaving ApplyGI the single exposure
  boundary. Neo's min(acc, 8) becomes SCENE_WRITER_CLAMP, applied while the
  value is still exposed. Both are exactly 1.0 / no-ops on the stock path.
- vRGB.w stays the reflecting pixel's scene linear depth, which is what
  DemosaicPS reads out of that channel; smoothness rides in HITPOS.w instead.
  Neo's reflected-depth term is deliberately not copied.
- The stage-1 provisional colour survives as debug view 6; any debug view clears
  the g-data flag so the debug picture is not overwritten by ShadePS.

Validated with an fxc harness over the real include closure: ShadePS with and
without the RT flags, BuildRayTracingLightListCS, ConeTracePS in four
permutations, DemosaicPS and UpScalePS - 0 errors.

